WEBVTT

NOTE Only the opening screen is an actual application screenshot. Other visuals are labeled illustrations or account instructions, not acceptance recordings.

1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.365
Welcome to CaseVant.

2
00:00:02.525 --> 00:00:03.625
Make your case.

3
00:00:03.785 --> 00:00:06.835
Evidence, options and outcomes, connected.

4
00:00:06.995 --> 00:00:12.640
In ten minutes, follow a case from import to review and reporting, then start your own.

5
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:19.495
This course uses the current CaseVant workspace, with a real opening screen and labeled workflow illustrations.

6
00:00:19.655 --> 00:00:24.155
Account instructions explain actions rather than claim recorded success.

7
00:00:24.315 --> 00:00:27.840
Practise with fictional or de-identified material.

8
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.745
Choose Demo to learn from fictional examples.

9
00:00:33.905 --> 00:00:40.530
Open Canopy overview for a guided starting point, or browse the available examples and simulations.

10
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:45.205
Choose Templates for a fresh draft with a case type and intake questions.

11
00:00:45.365 --> 00:00:47.555
Supply your own facts and evidence.

12
00:00:47.715 --> 00:00:55.185
Personal cases and Team records have different destinations; opening an example or template does not create a saved record.

13
00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:06.995
Our example is Five Flats, Three Borders, sometimes called Five Flats, Three Countries.

14
00:01:07.155 --> 00:01:12.075
Use the complete final Markdown file, including its embedded case data.

15
00:01:12.235 --> 00:01:15.620
From the entry screen, choose Import case or prompt.

16
00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:21.775
Inside the editor, the equivalent route is More actions, then Import case prompt, dot m d.

17
00:01:21.935 --> 00:01:25.135
Importing text is not yet applying its graph.

18
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.955
Choose Verify canonical case.

19
00:01:33.115 --> 00:01:39.355
This path checks the embedded structure and fingerprint locally, without asking AI to reinterpret the file.

20
00:01:39.515 --> 00:01:44.365
Review the verified title, version, twenty-three nodes and thirty-six relations.

21
00:01:44.525 --> 00:01:48.020
A matching fingerprint confirms which case data you have.

22
00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:54.855
It does not independently verify the evidence, legal conclusions, tax rates or any claimed review date.

23
00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:04.655
Choose Apply exact case when the verified preview matches your file.

24
00:02:04.815 --> 00:02:11.180
For a professional case, use Overview, Sources and evidence, Decision, Review, and Reports.

25
00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:15.665
Brief and structure contains Edit the brief and Review proposed changes.

26
00:02:15.825 --> 00:02:20.035
Training simulations retain their guided steps and play controls.

27
00:02:20.195 --> 00:02:24.930
These sections organize work; they do not confirm a save or independent approval.

28
00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:35.000
Read the title, jurisdiction, professional role and Case context.

29
00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:42.030
This fictional matter concerns a PRC-resident client, five English flats and a proposed Liechtenstein structure.

30
00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:46.955
The client's preferred structure is a request to investigate, not the answer.

31
00:02:47.115 --> 00:02:51.550
Keep alternative routes, unresolved questions and stop conditions visible.

32
00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:56.210
Preserve the original file before changing its reviewed working copy.

33
00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.495
Inspect the evidence and the decision it supports.

34
00:03:03.655 --> 00:03:09.000
For example, the KYC questionnaire connects to the ownership and funds investigation.

35
00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.940
A named evidence node is not proof that its underlying document has been accepted.

36
00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:19.585
Record what the source establishes, what remains uncertain, and which decision depends on it.

37
00:03:19.745 --> 00:03:23.600
Use case actions to return directly to missing information.

38
00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.890
Use the economics in the case you actually opened.

39
00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:38.170
Check purchase price, debt, interest, repayment basis and term.

40
00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:43.855
Then verify annual rent, operating expenses and structure costs against their sources.

41
00:03:44.015 --> 00:03:46.820
An older example may use different figures.

42
00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:52.280
When assumptions change, recalculate and inspect the result before relying on it.

43
00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:56.430
Keep the calculation basis and unresolved inputs visible.

44
00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.980
The requested ten-percent return needs a named measure.

45
00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:09.390
Gross yield, cash-on-cash return and equity I R R answer different questions.

46
00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:13.765
Compare the displayed calculations with their assumptions and source evidence.

47
00:04:13.925 --> 00:04:19.390
This file contains provisional acquisition costs and unverified tax-rate sources.

48
00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:26.000
We are demonstrating the review workflow, not confirming a tax advantage or promising that the target is achieved.

49
00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:33.420
Open Decision to inspect the decision map.

50
00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:38.925
Select a node, read its detail and follow its connections to the next question or outcome.

51
00:04:39.085 --> 00:04:44.360
In Five Flats, defining the return metric and checking lawful funding are meaningful gates.

52
00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:48.550
Follow a stop or renegotiation route as well as a proceeding route.

53
00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:51.605
Explain which evidence could change the decision.

54
00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:03.345
Open Review and read the checks for your case.

55
00:05:03.505 --> 00:05:07.765
Return to missing fields, evidence or connections and correct the draft.

56
00:05:07.925 --> 00:05:12.715
Training simulations also offer Test and Play controls when their routes are ready.

57
00:05:12.875 --> 00:05:16.780
A professional decision package does not need an artificial game route.

58
00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:23.585
Structural completeness is one check; evidence quality and professional judgment still require review.

59
00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:33.950
Open Reports or choose Create analytical report.

60
00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:40.565
The report dialog offers Preview PDF and Download PDF, with further settings and approval options.

61
00:05:40.725 --> 00:05:42.575
Begin with an internal draft.

62
00:05:42.735 --> 00:05:47.190
Inspect its identity, assumptions, evidence and decision map.

63
00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:50.420
Open the downloaded file to confirm delivery.

64
00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:55.185
A draft export does not create independent approval or a governed Team report.

65
00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:06.505
After choosing Download PDF, check your browser's downloads and open the file yourself.

66
00:06:06.665 --> 00:06:11.395
The message PDF download started confirms initiation, not delivery.

67
00:06:11.555 --> 00:06:18.720
To preserve an editable canonical handoff, use More actions, then Export Final case prompt, dot m d.

68
00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:21.390
Read its status controls carefully.

69
00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:27.640
A filename containing Final does not supply missing evidence or create independent reviewer approval.

70
00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:34.495
To save a personal case, choose Save to workspace.

71
00:06:34.655 --> 00:06:37.920
Sign in and complete your profile if prompted.

72
00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:43.825
Wait for Saved to workspace, then open My cases, Personal, with the same account.

73
00:06:43.985 --> 00:06:48.150
Check the restored content in a separate tab before closing the original.

74
00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:49.915
Team records are separate.

75
00:06:50.075 --> 00:06:55.215
These are account instructions; this course does not claim a recorded successful save.

76
00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:03.090
Now create your own fictional case.

77
00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:07.835
Preserve the current work first, return to Case Studio and choose Create a case.

78
00:07:07.995 --> 00:07:11.995
Read any replacement or unsaved-work prompt before proceeding.

79
00:07:12.155 --> 00:07:14.930
The new draft starts a separate authoring task.

80
00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:24.255
Alternatively, choose a suitable starter in Templates; review its case type and intake questions instead of treating the starter as a finished example.

81
00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:33.965
Open Brief and structure, then Edit the brief.

82
00:07:34.125 --> 00:07:40.020
Describe the people involved, decision, jurisdiction, known facts, evidence and deadline.

83
00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:45.540
For practice, ask whether a fictional business should approve a supplier change before launch.

84
00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.555
Mark prices and delivery claims as unverified until supported.

85
00:07:49.715 --> 00:07:54.550
State the alternatives and the conditions that would make you pause instead of proceeding.

86
00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:05.660
This optional AI path is an instruction, not a recorded authenticated request.

87
00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:10.735
Where enabled, Understand with AI requires sign-in and a confirmed profile.

88
00:08:10.895 --> 00:08:14.340
It proposes changes for review before you apply them.

89
00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:18.125
Check the current data-handling notice before sending material.

90
00:08:18.285 --> 00:08:26.835
If unavailable, continue with manual editing or the explicitly labeled local fallback; do not mistake fallback output for AI analysis.

91
00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:34.325
Complete Sources and evidence, then inspect Decision.

92
00:08:34.485 --> 00:08:38.750
Give nodes concrete titles and connect choices to reasoned outcomes.

93
00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:44.030
Use Review to identify structural gaps, then Reports to inspect the output.

94
00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:48.735
Save to workspace separately and verify the saved copy under Personal.

95
00:08:48.895 --> 00:08:52.040
Do not replace missing evidence with confident wording.

96
00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:57.490
A useful decision package explains both the recommendation and its unresolved conditions.

97
00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:05.750
For shared work, open My cases, Team, and select the intended organization.

98
00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:09.705
Use New case and complete the requested matter details.

99
00:09:09.865 --> 00:09:14.520
Verify the returned record and organization before adding documents or reviews.

100
00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:18.505
A personal Studio save does not create this Team record.

101
00:09:18.665 --> 00:09:22.420
These are account instructions, not a recorded creation.

102
00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:25.695
Your permissions determine the actions available.

103
00:09:30.650 --> 00:09:39.570
Practise importing and verifying a complete case file, tracing one evidence-dependent decision, inspecting a report and starting a fictional case.

104
00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:43.220
Confirm any save under My cases, Personal.

105
00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:50.110
If moving from the earlier domain, use the same account and preserve device-only drafts before closing that tab.

106
00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:53.335
Return to Help and training for current guides.

107
00:09:53.495 --> 00:09:56.185
Make your case with evidence you can explain.
